# The cross-tool contract goldens are hashed BYTE-FOR-BYTE and the hash is pinned in
# ContractFixturesTest (and byte-identically in the VS Code twin). Git for Windows
# installs with core.autocrlf=true by DEFAULT, which rewrites this file on checkout:
# the suite then fails on a clean clone before a single line is edited, and the failure
# message sends you to regenerate the fixture — which can never converge, because the
# generator writes LF and git hands it back as CRLF. Pasting the CRLF hash "fixes" it
# for that one machine and breaks every other one, desynchronising the very contract the
# file exists to freeze. Never translate it.
src/test/resources/clipboard-contract.json -text

# gradlew is executed by sh; CRLF makes it fail to start under git-bash / WSL.
gradlew text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
